<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia to cut telecoms tariffs for exporters.</title>
<headline>Tunisia to cut telecoms tariffs for exporters.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia on Monday announced it will cut telecommunications tariffs for exporters in order to encourage investment.</p>
<p>Communications Minister Habib Ammar said that telex tariffs will be cut by 40 percent, specialised traffic for data transfer by 30 to 40 percent and telephone calls by 14 percent.</p>
<p>He said the cuts applied only to firms fully exporting their production. He did not say when the new rates would be implemented.</p>
</text>
